AB  - About FAO News Multimedia Main topics Statistics Members Publications. ##### Share. ## Common Oceans Program. ##### Deep-sea fisheries. Deep-sea fisheries are an important source of employment and nutrition. They typically take place between depths of 200 and 1500 meters, targeting bottom-dwelling species on continental shelves, seamounts and ocean ridges using trawls, set gill nets, longlines and pots. Their careful management is vital because the target species are generally slow to reproduce which makes them particularly sensitive to overfishing. Additionally, as the gear frequently contact
